{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>And if you do not dispossess, etc., and it shall come to pass, etc.</b> According to the Sages, of blessed memory (Megillah 10b), who said that everywhere the expression ״וְהָיָה״ (\"and it shall come to pass\") is used, it is a language of joy — here the verse intends to say that even though they will allow them to remain out of desire and delight in them for their needs, He nevertheless proclaims to them that they shall become thorns in your sides, etc." "<b>And they shall harass you upon the land, etc.</b> Meaning: not only will they hold onto a portion of the land that you did not merit, but even the portion that you did merit and in which you settled and dwell — they will harass you upon the portion where you dwell, saying, ״Arise, get out of it.״ And the meaning of the word <b>upon</b> is as in His saying (Numbers 20:24) ״עַל אֲשֶׁר מְרִיתֶם פִּי״ (because you rebelled against My mouth), and ״עַל אֲשֶׁר לֹא קִדַּשְׁתֶם״ (Deuteronomy 32:51)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:10.675163971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}